; PORT.DEF - marks the port driver DYNAMICALLY LOADABLE and exports its DDB.
;
; The DDK sample ships no .DEF and its MAKEFILE links with /VXD /NOD only, which
; produces an LE image with module flags 0x00028000. Every .PDR that IOS
; actually loads on this machine - HSFLOP.PDR, RMM.PDR - carries 0x00038000.
; The extra bit is the dynamic-load marker, and IOS loads IOSUBSYS drivers
; dynamically, so without it the loader refuses the image before dispatching
; SYS_DYNAMIC_DEVICE_INIT. No control message, no IOS_Register, no probe - just
; "Init Failure" with none of our code having run. That was true from phase 0.
VXD PORT DYNAMIC

EXPORTS
	PORT_DDB	@1
